{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34676018",
      "title": "Preparing the Database",
      "lectureOrder": 90,
      "videoOrder": 83,
      "sourceHash": "7773606008f2f3ec8f235ca80c72d8d91091fdec40e12b71021dd388787b21ec",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.13,
          "end": 3.75,
          "en": "So, let's get started with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.75,
          "end": 5.46,
          "en": "implementing authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.46,
          "end": 7.23,
          "en": "For that, I'm back in the project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.23,
          "end": 9.03,
          "en": "I started my development server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.03,
          "end": 11.52,
          "en": "So I have the application up and running here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.52,
          "end": 15.39,
          "en": "And at the moment, of course, everyone can add new expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.39,
          "end": 17.91,
          "en": "For example, I can add a new expense here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.91,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "without being logged in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 23.97,
          "en": "Matter of fact, right now we have no login functionality",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.97,
          "end": 26.43,
          "en": "and therefore all these expenses are public,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.43,
          "end": 30.66,
          "en": "and global, and all users have the same expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.66,
          "end": 33.9,
          "en": "And throughout this section, we're going to change that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.9,
          "end": 37.14,
          "en": "We're going to protect access to this expense area",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.14,
          "end": 40.47,
          "en": "to only grant authenticated users access to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.47,
          "end": 45.06,
          "en": "And we'll make sure that every user has their own expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.06,
          "end": 47.193,
          "en": "so that we have no shared expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.18,
          "end": 49.013,
          "en": "We will of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.013,
          "end": 51.78,
          "en": "also make sure that the logout button does something,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.78,
          "end": 53.73,
          "en": "but for that we first of all must make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.73,
          "end": 58.08,
          "en": "that we can log in, and that we can create new users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 58.08,
          "end": 60.69,
          "en": "Because we need both functionalities.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.69,
          "end": 63.54,
          "en": "We must be able to create new users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.54,
          "end": 66.6,
          "en": "But of course existing users also must be able to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.6,
          "end": 68.91,
          "en": "authenticate and log in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.91,
          "end": 71.16,
          "en": "And therefore, to get started here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.16,
          "end": 76.16,
          "en": "it makes sense to start with the user creation process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.309,
          "end": 78.84,
          "en": "because we can only implement authentication and validate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.84,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "user credentials if we have users to begin with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 85.2,
          "en": "Now for that, back in our code base,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.2,
          "end": 87.49,
          "en": "I'm not going to start with some front end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.34100000000001,
          "end": 90.66,
          "en": "or back end React code or Remix code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.66,
          "end": 94.62,
          "en": "Instead, I'll get back to my prisma schema here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.62,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "Now you might recall that schema dot prisma file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 99.47999999999999,
          "en": "from the last course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.47999999999999,
          "end": 101.22,
          "en": "Prisma is a third party package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.22,
          "end": 102.75,
          "en": "which we're using here to interact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 102.75,
          "end": 104.37,
          "en": "with the Mongo Db Database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.37,
          "end": 105.72,
          "en": "And with that package,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 105.72,
          "end": 108.6,
          "en": "we basically describe our data models",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.6,
          "end": 113.03999999999999,
          "en": "and then Prisma makes sure that database queries are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.03999999999999,
          "end": 114.45,
          "en": "generated under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 114.45,
          "end": 118.53,
          "en": "and we talk to the database in a very convenient way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 118.53,
          "end": 121.65,
          "en": "Now we already have one model for expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 121.65,
          "end": 124.08,
          "en": "Now I'm going to add another model for users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 124.08,
          "end": 127.41,
          "en": "because now our application does not just know expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.41,
          "end": 129.36,
          "en": "but also users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 129.36,
          "end": 133.35,
          "en": "Now for those users, I want to have a unique user ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.35,
          "end": 136.98,
          "en": "per user, and that ID will be generated in the same way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 138.75,
          "en": "as we do it for expenses.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 138.75,
          "end": 142.773,
          "en": "So we have this Auto generated MongoDB specific ID here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.18,
          "end": 146.85,
          "en": "Then every user should have an email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.85,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "which is of type string, so which is some text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 152.103,
          "en": "and a password which is also some text in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 157.11,
          "en": "And then very important, every user also will have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 157.11,
          "end": 161.04,
          "en": "some expenses mapped to him or her.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.04,
          "end": 163.8,
          "en": "And for that, we'll add an expenses field here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 163.8,
          "end": 167.73,
          "en": "and that will be of type expense array written like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.73,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "If you now hit your auto format shortcut",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 172.17000000000002,
          "en": "in Visual Studio Code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.17000000000002,
          "end": 174.42000000000002,
          "en": "and you have this Prisma extension installed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.42000000000002,
          "end": 177.06,
          "en": "you should automatically get a nicer format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.06,
          "end": 180.3,
          "en": "And you should also get these two entries added to your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.3,
          "end": 183.15,
          "en": "expense model, because this is now a relation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.15,
          "end": 185.97,
          "en": "between these two models where every user has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 185.97,
          "end": 189,
          "en": "multiple expenses mapped to him or her,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 189,
          "end": 193.74,
          "en": "and every expense has one user assigned to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 193.74,
          "end": 196.14,
          "en": "If you don't have that extension, you can simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 196.14,
          "end": 199.953,
          "en": "manually add these two lines to your expense model.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 201.18,
          "end": 204.3,
          "en": "Now, I will actually remove these question marks here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 204.3,
          "end": 208.02,
          "en": "to make sure that it's not optional for expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.02,
          "end": 209.34,
          "en": "to be mapped to users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 209.34,
          "end": 212.22,
          "en": "Instead, every expense must be mapped to users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 212.22,
          "end": 214.07999999999998,
          "en": "And therefore I'll then save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 214.07999999999998,
          "end": 217.26,
          "en": "and then actually quit my development server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 222.21,
          "en": "and run NPX Prisma DB Push.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.21,
          "end": 224.13,
          "en": "And what this will do, this command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 226.05,
          "en": "which we haven't executed before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 226.05,
          "end": 229.07999999999998,
          "en": "is it will basically take these models",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 229.07999999999998,
          "end": 232.59,
          "en": "and apply them to our database, to the MongoDB database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 232.59,
          "end": 236.31,
          "en": "It will initialize the database for these models.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 236.31,
          "end": 238.38,
          "en": "We didn't have to do that before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 238.38,
          "end": 240.01,
          "en": "but now I will actually do it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 240.866,
          "end": 244.47,
          "en": "because I will add one extra field to my email entry here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 244.47,
          "end": 249.03,
          "en": "The @unique field, which ensures that emails are unique.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.03,
          "end": 251.31,
          "en": "And for that, when using MongoDB,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 251.31,
          "end": 253.71,
          "en": "we must generate a MongoDB index.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 253.71,
          "end": 257.19,
          "en": "We basically must enable a MongoDB feature that checks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.19,
          "end": 259.47,
          "en": "whether we have duplicate emails.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 259.47,
          "end": 261.6,
          "en": "And by running npx prisma db push,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 261.6,
          "end": 265.17,
          "en": "the database will be initialized accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 265.17,
          "end": 269.047,
          "en": "So after running this, our database is initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.047,
          "end": 272.181,
          "en": "and we can start that development server again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 272.181,
          "end": 274.83,
          "en": "And one thing I'll do now on my MongoDB back and here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 274.83,
          "end": 277.53,
          "en": "or on this MongoDB Atlas service,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 277.53,
          "end": 281.19,
          "en": "is I'll browse my collections, and there we have an expense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 281.19,
          "end": 282.42,
          "en": "and a user collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 282.42,
          "end": 284.04,
          "en": "And for my expense collection,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 284.04,
          "end": 286.44,
          "en": "I'll delete all expenses which I have there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 286.44,
          "end": 290.34000000000003,
          "en": "To clear my database because the new expenses which we'll",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 290.34000000000003,
          "end": 293.64,
          "en": "add will have some user details attached to them,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 293.64,
          "end": 296.04,
          "en": "and the old expenses don't have that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 296.04,
          "end": 297.81,
          "en": "But we want to have that for the future,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 297.81,
          "end": 300.9,
          "en": "hence the adjustment with that extra model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 300.9,
          "end": 303.78,
          "en": "and this npx prisma db push command,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 303.78,
          "end": 307.143,
          "en": "and hence me clearing that expense collection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 308.01,
          "end": 310.17,
          "en": "With that, the database is prepared though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 310.17,
          "end": 311.64,
          "en": "We have our user model,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 311.64,
          "end": 314.613,
          "en": "and we can therefore get started creating users.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
